# Workstation protocols and command restrictions (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08): **Must test all types of workstations
and protocols such as SSH, RDP, VNC. Must also test command
restrictions.** Chrome matrices and SSH-only PAW proofs are not
comprehensive Connect / PAM QA.

This rule extends
[`session-connect-protocol-surface.mdc`](session-connect-protocol-surface.mdc):
that rule defines *what* protocol-surface proof is; this rule requires
that proof **across every protocol and workstation type the lab offers**,
plus **live command governance**.

## The rule

> **Claims that Connect / Open / Launch / workstation access “works,” or
> that comprehensive PAM / session QA is done, MUST include
> protocol-surface proof (per
> [`session-connect-protocol-surface.mdc`](session-connect-protocol-surface.mdc))
> for each protocol the lab seats offer among SSH, RDP, and VNC — not
> SSH-only. Agents MUST inventory lab workstation types present
> (Docker / Hyper-V / physical / Windows / Linux / macOS) and prove or
> honest-BLOCK each type. Command restrictions (SSH command filtering /
> command governance) MUST be exercised live: an allowlisted command
> succeeds and a restricted command is denied — not chrome-only on
> `/pam/command-governance`. Single-protocol or single-seat PASS
> matrices are forbidden as “all protocols / all workstations” green.**

## When this rule applies

Trigger phrases (non-exhaustive): comprehensive test, full product /
PAM / session QA, Connect works, Open / Launch works, all workstations
tested, SSH/RDP/VNC coverage, command governance / command restrictions
tested, My Workstations matrix complete.

Does **not** force multi-protocol fan-out for a narrowly scoped chrome
layout fix that explicitly scopes out session workflows (still must not
claim Connect or multi-protocol coverage).

## Required protocol matrix

Before claiming Connect / PAM session coverage is complete:

| Protocol | Proof bar (each offered by lab) |
| --- | --- |
| **SSH** | Protocol-surface: non-zero session id + `.xterm` / `live-ssh-terminal` + status `connecting\|connected` on a named SSH seat |
| **RDP** | Protocol-surface: non-zero session id + `live-rdp-canvas` / canvas + status `connecting\|connected` on a named RDP seat (e.g. Lab Hyper-V Windows CUI) |
| **VNC** | Protocol-surface: non-zero session id + `live-vnc-canvas` / canvas + status `connecting\|connected` on a named VNC seat |

- If the lab **offers** a protocol (seeded seat / connection point with
  that protocol chip), that row is **required** PASS or honest
  **BLOCKED** with reason — never silently omitted.
- If a protocol has **no** lab seat this run, record **N/A — no seat**
  with inventory evidence; do not invent PASS from another protocol.
- SSH-only Docker PAW proof **never** green-lights RDP or VNC.

Canonical patterns (examples, not exclusive):

- SSH: `ui/e2e/my-workstations-connect-paw-embedded-live.spec.ts`
- RDP: `ui/e2e/my-workstations-connect-rdp-embedded-live.spec.ts`
- Multi-entry: `ui/e2e/connect-all-entrypoints-embedded-live.spec.ts`

## Required workstation-type inventory

Before claiming “all workstations” or comprehensive My Workstations QA:

1. **Inventory** seats present in the lab (API list and/or UI cards):
   Docker Linux PAM PAW, Hyper-V Windows / Linux, physical hosts,
   Windows / Linux / macOS — whichever exist this run.
2. For **each type present**, either:
   - **PASS** with protocol-surface proof on a named seat of that type, or
   - **BLOCKED** with a one-line reason (seat down, no Jump capacity,
     WA missing, etc.).
3. **Forbidden:** claiming all types from one Linux SSH PAW row.

## Required command-restriction exercise

Before claiming command governance / command restrictions tested:

| # | Exercise | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **Allowlisted command** | In a live governed SSH session (or documented governance path), an allowed command runs successfully |
| 2 | **Restricted command** | A denied / filtered command is rejected with a clear deny (UI and/or session feedback) — not merely HTTP 200 on a settings page |
| 3 | **Not chrome-only** | Nav to `/pam/command-governance` or heading asserts alone is **FAIL** for this claim |

If governance cannot be exercised (no policy bound, session broker
down): mark **BLOCKED** — do not PASS from page load.

## Forbidden “false green”

Do **not** treat any of these as multi-protocol / multi-type / command-
restriction success:

- SSH-only protocol-surface PASS cited as “Connect works” for RDP/VNC
- Single-seat matrix generalized to all workstation types
- Jump / Session Control / Connection points chrome without per-protocol
  protocol-surface rows
- `/pam/command-governance` crawl without allow + deny live exercise
- Mocked workstation lists or chrome-only Connect specs
- Binder / nav crawl PASS matrices without the protocol × type table

## Required agent behavior

1. When claiming comprehensive Connect / PAM session QA: publish a short
   matrix — protocol (SSH/RDP/VNC) × workstation type — each cell
   PASS / BLOCKED / N/A with evidence path or e2e name.
2. Cross-link
   [`session-connect-protocol-surface.mdc`](session-connect-protocol-surface.mdc)
   for the per-cell proof bar.
3. Prefer leaving `aic-server-service` Running; never rotate **`phil`**;
   no `cargo clean`.
4. Preflight checklist:
   `pim-offline-server/docs/dev/comprehensive-test-preflight-checklist-20260805.md`
   (Gate 4+ multi-protocol / command-restriction rows).

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation:** “Connect / PAM session 22/22 PASS” from Docker Linux SSH
PAW xterm + Jump chrome + `/pam/command-governance` heading visible.
No RDP/VNC surface, no Hyper-V Windows seat, no allow/deny command
proof.

**Fix:** Inventory seats → protocol-surface PASS (or BLOCKED) for SSH
**and** every offered RDP/VNC seat type → live allowlisted command OK +
restricted command denied → matrix in evidence README. Chrome-only and
SSH-only rows stay labeled chrome-only / SSH-only.

